      "text": "To compute the overall mean of her class, they must sum all of her students' test scores then divide by the number of test scores.\nThe first black students have scores of 72% then we will add that to the second, and third, and so on...\n\nAll the first black students scores:\n\n\\[72 + 72 + 72 + 72 + 72 + 72 + 72 = 432\\]\n\nThe second black students scores:\n\n\\[78 + 78 + 78 + 78 + 78 + 78 = 468\\]\n\nThe total black students will add to 432 and 468 to will equal 900.\n\nDivide 900 by 36 to get new mean of the class. \n\nWhen calculating the equation, they should be adding graduates:\n\n```python\nThe total black students will add to 432, 468,\nand hence the new classes mean\n```\n\nThus, their class new total will equal 900, then divide the class mean by 36:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total} = 900 \\div 36 = 25 \\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, their class mean is $\\boxed{25\\%}$.",
